// An import without .* does not bring names in: they are written with its name in front. A bare
// one is found when the program is checked.
import NsShapes
print(NsShapes.PI_ISH)
print(PI_ISH)
// expect compile error: error_ns_bare.astra:5:7: error: 'PI_ISH' is written NsShapes.PI_ISH here: the import has no .*, so its names are not in reach by themselves
